Fix AOT compatibility warnings in the following non-serialization files in `/tmp/sv-415b2e1bbd5e4692ac0c3a67361576b1/before/`. Do NOT run builds - just make the edits.

## 1. ArmOperation.cs (IL2087, IL2090)

The `IsResource<T>()` method uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` without DynamicallyAccessedMembers on T.

Also, `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>` call IsResource<T>(), and `GenericOperationSource<T>` is instantiated with T in those methods.

Fix: Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the T parameter on `IsResource<T>()`, and propagate to `Rehydrate<T>()` and `RehydrateAsync<T>()`.

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the usings.

The annotation should appear on the T constraint: change `where T : notnull` to include the attribute on the type parameter.

Example:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

Do the same for `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>`.

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs (IL2087)

The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`.

`ModelReaderWriter.Read` requires `DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors` on the type.
`Activator.CreateInstance` requires `DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors`.

Fix: Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the T type parameter of the class.

```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

Also add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not already present (it IS already there, check first).

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs (IL2026, IL3050)

The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` at line 30 calls `RegisterClientFactory` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. Since this is fundamentally trim-incompatible (configuration binding), mark the method:

```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(...)
```

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the usings.

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs (IL2026, IL3050) - line 80

`ToString()` uses `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)`. Replace with manual JSON construction using Utf8JsonWriter:

```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    using var stream = new System.IO.MemoryStream();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(stream))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint?.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteString("DefaultScope", DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(stream.ToArray());
}
```

Add `using System.IO;` and `using System.Text;` if not already there. Keep `using System.Text.Json;` since it's needed for Utf8JsonWriter.

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs (IL2026, IL3050) - line 52

`JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` - replace with JsonDocument parsing:

The current code:
